<title>GERMANY: Issing says German 97 deficit could meet EMU limit.</title>
<headline>Issing says German 97 deficit could meet EMU limit.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank director Otmar Issing said on Thursday it was possible that Germany could meet the budget deficit criteria for the single European currency in 1997.</p>
<p>Issing said it may be possible for Germany to cut its budget deficit to 2.5 percent in 1997, well below the 3.0 percent upper limit to qualify for the Maastrict criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;A deficit criteria of 2.5 percent would be possible,&quot; Issing said. &quot;That is not to say 2.5 percent will be the level.&quot;</p>
<p>He said that the Bundesbank is very concerned about creative accounting practices being used in some European countries in order to qualify for monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;Reaching the criteria cannot be a one-off,&quot; he said. &quot;It has to be lasting.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 260 970</p>
</text>
